# Accessibility & UX (Frontend)

## Purpose

Ship interfaces usable by default — WCAG 2.1 AA as target unless project specifies otherwise.

## Accessibility Checklist

- [ ] Semantic HTML (`button` not `div onClick`, `nav`, `main`, `heading` hierarchy)
- [ ] Keyboard navigable: focus order, visible focus ring, Escape closes modals
- [ ] Labels: every input has associated `<label>` or `aria-label`
- [ ] Images: meaningful `alt` text; decorative `alt=""`
- [ ] Color: contrast ≥ 4.5:1 for text; don't rely on color alone
- [ ] Live regions for async feedback (`aria-live` for toasts/errors)
- [ ] Forms: associate errors with fields (`aria-describedby`, `aria-invalid`)

## UX Standards

- Loading: skeleton or spinner — never blank screen during fetch.
- Errors: actionable message + retry when applicable.
- Destructive actions: confirmation dialog.
- Empty states: explain what to do next.

## Forms

- Disable submit during in-flight request; show progress.
- Validate on blur/submit per project pattern — always show field-level errors.
- Preserve user input on server error.

## Internationalization

- Externalize user-visible strings when i18n is in project scope.
- Avoid concatenating translated fragments — use interpolation.

## Testing A11y

- Run axe or eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y in CI when configured.
- Manual keyboard pass for new interactive flows.